💭 test: unoptimized
💭 A 🍯 of 60 keys has keys that share buckets whatever the seed of the string hashes. Copying it when one of the copies
💭 is changed copies the bucket storage, which must keep every entry of every chain. The original is checked after the
💭 copy is changed and the copy before (#247, the bug of 877bdfb4 lost entries only for some seeds).
